  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nThe current parent solution provides a baseline for improvement. The approach involves using a restricted set of basis functions to parameterize the step function, allowing global optimization via gradient descent on a convex relaxation of the problem. This addresses the non-convex nature by projecting solutions to enforce the unit area constraint while minimizing the max-correlation upper bound. The method systematically explores multiple starting points while ensuring feasibility and improving upon the record value.\n\nRationale:\n(a) The basis-function approach reduces dimensionality while maintaining solution quality\n(b) Projection ensures strict satisfaction of integral constraint through optimization\n(c) Multi-start minimization avoids local optima\n(d) Straightforward gradient-based optimization\n\nKey bottleneck addressed: Need better methodology than parent's complex multi-step phases\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n- Objective: Minimize C5 = dx * max_{k} \u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\n- Representation: h(x) = \u03a3_{i=1}^m w_i * \u03c6_i(x) where \u03c6_i are base functions\n- Constraints: 0 \u2264 w_i \u2264 1, \u03a3_{i=1}^m w_i * \u222b\u03c6_i(x)dx = 1, and \u03a3_{i=1}^m w_i * \u222b\u03c6_i(x+k)dx \u2264 1 \u2200k\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nParent Validation:\n- Accept initial_h_values if available, convert to dense array if needed\n- Create feasible initial guess through exponential transformation\n\nBasis Function Selection:\n- Define piecewise-polynomial basis functions with continuity constraints\n- Compute basis function integrals as constants\n\nAlgorithm:\ndef minimize_erdos():\n    1. Generate candidate basis from parent with added Gaussian noise\n    2. Create multiple shifted versions of basis (n-shifted = n\u00b110, n\u00b150, n\u00b1100, n\u00b1150)\n    3. Set descent direction = -\u2207f(x)\n    4. Update candidate with line search ensuring validity\n    5. Project new candidate to maintain integral constraint\n    6. Roulette-wheel select next candidate based on f(x)\n    7. Iterate until time exceeds budget\n\n4. Search Choices:\n- Warm-start with initial_h_values if available\n- Five primary shifts: \u00b110, \u00b150, \u00b1100, \u00b1150\n- Line search alpha=0.001 to 1e-4, beta=0.5 for projections\n- Basis resolution: np.linspace(0,2,n) for n=200-600\n- Time budget: 500s for optimization, 600s for testing\n\n5. Compute Budget:\nPhase1 (Warm-start): 300s for initial optimization\nPhase2 (Multi-start): 400s for 5 independent optimizations\nPhase3 (Final Polish): 400s for gradient-based polishing\n\n6. Validation:\n- Ensure 0\u2264h_i\u22641 by projection\n- Maintain \u2211h_i*dx = 1 exactly through projection\n- Compute C5 exactly and keep historical best\n- Return with \u03b1_ij selection if time permits.",
